(1052939, 126166, 25742, '<td valign="top">I like this. funny and cool</td>', 'I like this. funny and cool', '2004-12-08 18:57:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1052940, 125150, 6999, '<td valign="top">like this - particularly your inclusion, and so strongly, of the fence - adds a sinister edge ot it, and takes it away from the bland shot it might otherwise have been. It has a feeling of ... well, not out-of-focus, but of not being quite sharp, and it bothers my vision a little.</td>', 'like this - particularly your inclusion, and so strongly, of the fence - adds a sinister edge ot it, and takes it away from the bland shot it might otherwise have been. It has a feeling of ... well, not out-of-focus, but of not being quite sharp, and it bothers my vision a little.', '2004-12-08 18:57:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1052941, 125073, 25742, '<td valign="top">something shouts: too much PS</td>', 'something shouts: too much PS', '2004-12-08 18:58:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1052948, 126295, 6999, '<td valign="top">Ooh but there''s some weird artefactness going down here. It seems to be straight-out-of-camera aspect ratio, so I''m fairly confident in suggesting your post-rocessing is letting you down a fair bit.<br/> <br/>Aside from which (and I expect most people will only have commented on the blocky sky), I think you have the beginnings of a good shot here - but only the beginning, I''m afraid: I like the idea of including some foreground interest, in that wall and cactus, but you seem to have had to stretch things to include them and thus relegated the interest in your main subject too much - that cactus is almost as strong a presence as the castle, and that surely isn''t what you intended. But you have at least not presented a head on boring shot just of the castle, so points for that. Is it worth my suggesting you have a look round and see how other similar compsitions have been worked?</td>', 'Ooh but there''s some weird artefactness going down here. It seems to be straight-out-of-camera aspect ratio, so I''m fairly confident in suggesting your post-rocessing is letting you down a fair bit. Aside from which (and I expect most people will only have commented on the blocky sky), I think you have the beginnings of a good shot here - but only the beginning, I''m afraid: I like the idea of including some foreground interest, in that wall and cactus, but you seem to have had to stretch things to include them and thus relegated the interest in your main subject too much - that cactus is almost as strong a presence as the castle, and that surely isn''t what you intended. But you have at least not presented a head on boring shot just of the castle, so points for that. Is it worth my suggesting you have a look round and see how other similar compsitions have been worked?', '2004-12-08 19:03:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1052955, 126221, 6999, '<td valign="top">Hurrah hurrah - some context at last. I feel like giving you extra points just for that, after the last few images. I wonder if you haven''t relegated your landmark too much for most tastes - and if the forground isn''t too cluttered and busy. I think that would be my personal criticism of it too - whilst you''ve captured the sense of the way it dominates the streets, I wonder if you haven''t just taken it too far. Good work.</td>', 'Hurrah hurrah - some context at last. I feel like giving you extra points just for that, after the last few images. I wonder if you haven''t relegated your landmark too much for most tastes - and if the forground isn''t too cluttered and busy. I think that would be my personal criticism of it too - whilst you''ve captured the sense of the way it dominates the streets, I wonder if you haven''t just taken it too far. Good work.', '2004-12-08 19:08:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1052958, 125442, 6999, '<td valign="top">Classical, neatly organised - filling the negative space with trees is always effective, and makes a useful lead into the top of the dome. Clever composition, and strong sense of plasticity in the dome itself.</td>', 'Classical, neatly organised - filling the negative space with trees is always effective, and makes a useful lead into the top of the dome. Clever composition, and strong sense of plasticity in the dome itself.', '2004-12-08 19:09:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1052964, 125874, 6999, '<td valign="top">Looks to have suffered from rather heavy processing  - whether or not in camera is impossible to tell, but to my eye it harms the shot a great deal. I think there might have been a strong sense of serenity, of early evening peace to it - that shade of blue - but it does need that cleanliness of image to go with the clean (and strong) composition.</td>', 'Looks to have suffered from rather heavy processing  - whether or not in camera is impossible to tell, but to my eye it harms the shot a great deal. I think there might have been a strong sense of serenity, of early evening peace to it - that shade of blue - but it does need that cleanliness of image to go with the clean (and strong) composition.', '2004-12-08 19:11:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1052969, 126289, 6999, '<td valign="top">The lines of the cables are fun - the lines of the streetlights are not so much. There''s some good feel here, in the steelwork, but I do wish the streetlights weren''t quite so intrusive.</td>', 'The lines of the cables are fun - the lines of the streetlights are not so much. There''s some good feel here, in the steelwork, but I do wish the streetlights weren''t quite so intrusive.', '2004-12-08 19:13:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1052977, 126177, 6999, '<td valign="top">This is a vile vile thing to do to anyone - you deserve censure in the extreme. In fact, you ought to be forced to live on the evil stuff for a month, then see if you''d be so keen on putting up a bloody great picture of the damnable logo. You swine.<br/> <br/>Rant over, this is in my opinion the best entry I''ve seen so far - cunning, beautifully composed, startling, different, and even the border works wonderfully. But I still really really really hope it doesn''t get onto the front page. Please, no ... please, no ... but I have to give you an 8, and trust that others wont.</td>', 'This is a vile vile thing to do to anyone - you deserve censure in the extreme. In fact, you ought to be forced to live on the evil stuff for a month, then see if you''d be so keen on putting up a bloody great picture of the damnable logo. You swine. Rant over, this is in my opinion the best entry I''ve seen so far - cunning, beautifully composed, startling, different, and even the border works wonderfully. But I still really really really hope it doesn''t get onto the front page. Please, no ... please, no ... but I have to give you an 8, and trust that others wont.', '2004-12-08 19:18:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1052985, 126252, 30214, '<td valign="top">dull photo, cropping is odd.</td>', 'dull photo, cropping is odd.', '2004-12-08 19:21:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1052994, 126274, 30214, '<td valign="top">I like the lighting</td>', 'I like the lighting', '2004-12-08 19:25:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1052995, 125693, 6999, '<td valign="top">Reflections always work well for centred compsitions.</td>', 'Reflections always work well for centred compsitions.', '2004-12-08 19:25:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1052999, 126298, 6999, '<td valign="top">Interesting shot - though your yellows might have been saturated a touch too much for me: that sense of partial over-exposure in the brickwork. The noise in the sky is a pity, though I expect in the building areas it''s actually helping you.</td>', 'Interesting shot - though your yellows might have been saturated a touch too much for me: that sense of partial over-exposure in the brickwork. The noise in the sky is a pity, though I expect in the building areas it''s actually helping you.', '2004-12-08 19:28:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1053008, 125054, 6999, '<td valign="top">Twice? Don''t get it ... strong image, good lines, clean, etc. etc.</td>', 'Twice? Don''t get it ... strong image, good lines, clean, etc. etc.', '2004-12-08 19:30:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1053094, 126202, 6667, '<td valign="top">Nicely done.  Clean and crisp.  Only comment. . . I might have gotten rid of the moon.  It seems that for all the boldness of this shot your eye is drawn to the moon.  BOL  Still a 6</td>', 'Nicely done.  Clean and crisp.  Only comment. . . I might have gotten rid of the moon.  It seems that for all the boldness of this shot your eye is drawn to the moon.  BOL  Still a 6', '2004-12-08 20:27:02.000000', NULL, 1),
