(1054179, 125336, 30224, '<td valign="top">Stunning colours.</td>', 'Stunning colours.', '2004-12-09 09:55:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054182, 125827, 30224, '<td valign="top">I think there''s too much here for the eye to really make an impact photograph. The subject is unusual however. But the scene seems a bit blurry?</td>', 'I think there''s too much here for the eye to really make an impact photograph. The subject is unusual however. But the scene seems a bit blurry?', '2004-12-09 09:56:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054183, 125425, 30224, '<td valign="top">Serene. Lovely. Full of flow.</td>', 'Serene. Lovely. Full of flow.', '2004-12-09 09:57:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054185, 126185, 30224, '<td valign="top">Interesting subject, but the light seems uninteresting as it does not really bring out any of the clock''s colours or shadows. Overcast days are tough though....</td>', 'Interesting subject, but the light seems uninteresting as it does not really bring out any of the clock''s colours or shadows. Overcast days are tough though....', '2004-12-09 09:59:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054205, 126226, 22479, '<td valign="top">I think the lighthouse was artistically composed. A technical detail which makes this photograph unacceptable to me is obvious cloning evident along the right edge nearby the edge of the railing around the lighthouse. I suggest examining the image at 300% and with boosted levels to carefully screen for such imperfections.<br/> <br/>Edit: The spot in question is just to the right of the bright railing. There is a circular artifact which may represent a stray healing/cloning brush stroke which I''m sure was inadvertently placed. The artifact is about 40 or so pixels in diameter. Very subtle but on my LCD screen it really pops out.<br/> <br/>Otherwise I feel the image is exposed nicely with good sharp focus. The reflection off the water is also a nice touch. On second thought, this deserves a bump up in score. :)</td>', 'I think the lighthouse was artistically composed. A technical detail which makes this photograph unacceptable to me is obvious cloning evident along the right edge nearby the edge of the railing around the lighthouse. I suggest examining the image at 300% and with boosted levels to carefully screen for such imperfections. Edit: The spot in question is just to the right of the bright railing. There is a circular artifact which may represent a stray healing/cloning brush stroke which I''m sure was inadvertently placed. The artifact is about 40 or so pixels in diameter. Very subtle but on my LCD screen it really pops out. Otherwise I feel the image is exposed nicely with good sharp focus. The reflection off the water is also a nice touch. On second thought, this deserves a bump up in score. :)', '2004-12-09 10:16:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054209, 126240, 22479, '<td valign="top">I am speechless. This is absolutely stunning and an instant winner in my book. I am interested in hearing your story for this shot. What strikes me most is the clarity of the moon set against the background of clouds. Did you boost the levels of the clouds to bring out more of the shadow details? <br/> <br/>I think the position in the sky as well as the centered composition really works well here.</td>', 'I am speechless. This is absolutely stunning and an instant winner in my book. I am interested in hearing your story for this shot. What strikes me most is the clarity of the moon set against the background of clouds. Did you boost the levels of the clouds to bring out more of the shadow details?  I think the position in the sky as well as the centered composition really works well here.', '2004-12-09 10:19:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054213, 125627, 22479, '<td valign="top">I think you hit the exposure on this shot perfectly. This is simply elegant. The levels on the bridge, water, sky, and buildings are all very well balanced. So clear, sharp, and focused.</td>', 'I think you hit the exposure on this shot perfectly. This is simply elegant. The levels on the bridge, water, sky, and buildings are all very well balanced. So clear, sharp, and focused.', '2004-12-09 10:22:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054214, 124710, 22479, '<td valign="top">A wonderful day to shoot the bridge. I was in SF this week and it was only rainy and cloudy. :( <br/> <br/>Love the sky and the saturation of colors in the water. This belongs on a postcard.</td>', 'A wonderful day to shoot the bridge. I was in SF this week and it was only rainy and cloudy. :(  Love the sky and the saturation of colors in the water. This belongs on a postcard.', '2004-12-09 10:22:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054215, 126214, 4226, '<td valign="top">this photo seems to have a lot of potential. first you can reduce some noise.. and well when converting to black and white, try to increase the contrast.... also a little on the low key would do great.. just my   suggestions...</td>', 'this photo seems to have a lot of potential. first you can reduce some noise.. and well when converting to black and white, try to increase the contrast.... also a little on the low key would do great.. just my   suggestions...', '2004-12-09 10:23:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054216, 125854, 22479, '<td valign="top">Great colors and hues. The relevance of the title escapes me though. Overall a wonderfully picturesque composition.<br/> <br/>Edit: Bumping up.</td>', 'Great colors and hues. The relevance of the title escapes me though. Overall a wonderfully picturesque composition. Edit: Bumping up.', '2004-12-09 10:25:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054218, 126242, 4226, '<td valign="top">Is this the lighthouse on CA1 ? just curious</td>', 'Is this the lighthouse on CA1 ? just curious', '2004-12-09 10:26:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054232, 126041, 22479, '<td valign="top">You chose a wonderful subject for your entry. I think the composition is excellent and framed very well with a pleasing perspective. A couple of comments...Slightly overexposed evidenced by loss of highlights nearby the lights. Other comment is that the depth of focus appears to be too shallow evidenced by loss of focus in the background, and particularly the far tower. Not sure what type of camera you are using, and perhaps the DOF is not easily adjustable. The exposure could have been reduced with a faster shutter, smaller aperture (increasing DOF as well), decreased exposure compensation, or decreased ISO sensitivity.</td>', 'You chose a wonderful subject for your entry. I think the composition is excellent and framed very well with a pleasing perspective. A couple of comments...Slightly overexposed evidenced by loss of highlights nearby the lights. Other comment is that the depth of focus appears to be too shallow evidenced by loss of focus in the background, and particularly the far tower. Not sure what type of camera you are using, and perhaps the DOF is not easily adjustable. The exposure could have been reduced with a faster shutter, smaller aperture (increasing DOF as well), decreased exposure compensation, or decreased ISO sensitivity.', '2004-12-09 10:37:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054295, 126146, 6999, '<td valign="top">My first thought here is to wonderr why you shot this from this point fo view: it seems to me thhat it doesn''t allow us much sense of the bridge at all. The head-high shot means that the intricacies of tthe ''roof'' are squeezed into very little space in your shot, and your angle to the thing means thhat the sides are similarly stuck for space - there''s almost more road here than brisge, and yet you haven''t given much impression of where it is at all - a bridge over what? How big is that river? How deep is the drop? There''s a strong sense of the bright colour of it, and that is well done, and the overall exposure is good - low enough for the colour to pop, but not so as to lose detail. Some experimentation with angles would help I think - even getting down on one knee to shoot can give an image just that bit of difference it needs to stand out. Good luck.</td>', 'My first thought here is to wonderr why you shot this from this point fo view: it seems to me thhat it doesn''t allow us much sense of the bridge at all. The head-high shot means that the intricacies of tthe ''roof'' are squeezed into very little space in your shot, and your angle to the thing means thhat the sides are similarly stuck for space - there''s almost more road here than brisge, and yet you haven''t given much impression of where it is at all - a bridge over what? How big is that river? How deep is the drop? There''s a strong sense of the bright colour of it, and that is well done, and the overall exposure is good - low enough for the colour to pop, but not so as to lose detail. Some experimentation with angles would help I think - even getting down on one knee to shoot can give an image just that bit of difference it needs to stand out. Good luck.', '2004-12-09 11:30:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054304, 126228, 6999, '<td valign="top">Well exposed, and there''s good detail, and a good capture of the light. I find the composition very weak however - so centred, so much negative space, so little else to guide the eye, and all of that with a quite ''ordinary'' seeming viewpoint - sure, it could be the most difficult view to get at in the world, but we don''t know that. You need, I feel, and especially with such architectural shots, to add some element of difference, or of the spectacular, of of the location. the building is interesting - that doesn''t automatically make the photograph interesting.</td>', 'Well exposed, and there''s good detail, and a good capture of the light. I find the composition very weak however - so centred, so much negative space, so little else to guide the eye, and all of that with a quite ''ordinary'' seeming viewpoint - sure, it could be the most difficult view to get at in the world, but we don''t know that. You need, I feel, and especially with such architectural shots, to add some element of difference, or of the spectacular, of of the location. the building is interesting - that doesn''t automatically make the photograph interesting.', '2004-12-09 11:34:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054309, 126262, 6999, '<td valign="top">Not sure about the perspective distortion, and you angling of the shot to keep the Empire State vretical at such expense to the other buildings. I think that more compsromise would have been acceptable, but that''s difficult to be certain of without trying it. There are also tools to help correct such phenomena, though they can be tricky to use.<br/> <br/>And something''s gone badly wrong ith the processing somewhere, I feel - or even if it''s deliberate, it just looks like a mistake. All those jagged lines, and compression artefacts ... and using just under a third of the available data.</td>', 'Not sure about the perspective distortion, and you angling of the shot to keep the Empire State vretical at such expense to the other buildings. I think that more compsromise would have been acceptable, but that''s difficult to be certain of without trying it. There are also tools to help correct such phenomena, though they can be tricky to use. And something''s gone badly wrong ith the processing somewhere, I feel - or even if it''s deliberate, it just looks like a mistake. All those jagged lines, and compression artefacts ... and using just under a third of the available data.', '2004-12-09 11:37:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054313, 126212, 6999, '<td valign="top">I guess that depends exactly how far east you''re prepared to go, really. I can see the appeal of this light and tonality, which is well captured. I don''t get the use of the odd angle, which seems neither a deliberate tilt nor an advantage. I like that you''ve tried a detail shot, rather than a dull full-on shot of as much of the building as you could get in ... but this seems oddly isolated. I think it''s a composition thing: might you still have held the sign as your primary subject, but used the lines of the rest of the frontage, or rather ''some more'' of the frontage, to bring the eye more strongly to that subject?</td>', 'I guess that depends exactly how far east you''re prepared to go, really. I can see the appeal of this light and tonality, which is well captured. I don''t get the use of the odd angle, which seems neither a deliberate tilt nor an advantage. I like that you''ve tried a detail shot, rather than a dull full-on shot of as much of the building as you could get in ... but this seems oddly isolated. I think it''s a composition thing: might you still have held the sign as your primary subject, but used the lines of the rest of the frontage, or rather ''some more'' of the frontage, to bring the eye more strongly to that subject?', '2004-12-09 11:40:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054315, 126014, 6999, '<td valign="top">Made me smile. I like the warm/cold light approach, though here, with this particular angle, I wonder that it doesn''t serve to over-accentuate the rigidty of that choice. It has a sense of lacking detail that isn''t solely down to the casting of the little model, either - it may be camera, or it may be processing, or it may be a non-tripod shot, or non-sharpening, but it hasn''t got that clarity of fine detail, that immediacy.</td>', 'Made me smile. I like the warm/cold light approach, though here, with this particular angle, I wonder that it doesn''t serve to over-accentuate the rigidty of that choice. It has a sense of lacking detail that isn''t solely down to the casting of the little model, either - it may be camera, or it may be processing, or it may be a non-tripod shot, or non-sharpening, but it hasn''t got that clarity of fine detail, that immediacy.', '2004-12-09 11:43:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054317, 125437, 6999, '<td valign="top">Pretty good allround. A touch over-exposed for the whiteness, and your crop has crowded the bottom the image for me. Good colours, pleasant composition.</td>', 'Pretty good allround. A touch over-exposed for the whiteness, and your crop has crowded the bottom the image for me. Good colours, pleasant composition.', '2004-12-09 11:45:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054327, 126029, 6999, '<td valign="top">There''s something really peculiar about this shot - there seem to be striations running vertically through the image, which I can''t understand. There''s also a sense of blockiness to it, throughout tthe lighthouse textures. Great image though - and controlling the burn-out from the light must have been a hell of a task, and there''s only minor distortion around it. Not convinced by your composition quite - the light seems placed neither centrally nor privileged, and I think that adds an unease to what ought to be a simple and elegant shot.</td>', 'There''s something really peculiar about this shot - there seem to be striations running vertically through the image, which I can''t understand. There''s also a sense of blockiness to it, throughout tthe lighthouse textures. Great image though - and controlling the burn-out from the light must have been a hell of a task, and there''s only minor distortion around it. Not convinced by your composition quite - the light seems placed neither centrally nor privileged, and I think that adds an unease to what ought to be a simple and elegant shot.', '2004-12-09 11:59:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054329, 125374, 6999, '<td valign="top">Impeccable, for me. A great eye, and i wish more people had put the thought into the composition of their images that you display here. Top so far.</td>', 'Impeccable, for me. A great eye, and i wish more people had put the thought into the composition of their images that you display here. Top so far.', '2004-12-09 12:02:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054332, 126159, 22970, '<td valign="top">Your photograph has very nice colors, lighting, focus, and perspective. Good Job!</td>', 'Your photograph has very nice colors, lighting, focus, and perspective. Good Job!', '2004-12-09 12:13:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054334, 126297, 27605, '<td valign="top">Nice warm light on the stone, good use of shadows to enhance lettering.  Also like the low perspective.  Background buildings are slightly distracting.</td>', 'Nice warm light on the stone, good use of shadows to enhance lettering.  Also like the low perspective.  Background buildings are slightly distracting.', '2004-12-09 12:13:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054336, 126121, 22970, '<td valign="top">I know this photograph must be a hard one to get just right. You dont want to get up close because you loose the dome on top but by taking the photograph from afar you loose out on emotion. But I feel under the circumstance you done a good job. Nice lighting, color, and focus. Good job!</td>', 'I know this photograph must be a hard one to get just right. You dont want to get up close because you loose the dome on top but by taking the photograph from afar you loose out on emotion. But I feel under the circumstance you done a good job. Nice lighting, color, and focus. Good job!', '2004-12-09 12:17:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054339, 125437, 22970, '<td valign="top">Hi, I like your photograph for several reasons. The shadows are nice giving lines and making the overall photograph more interesting and your lighting is good. But the focus seems to be off. Maybe camera shake, I dont know but it seems not to be crisp. Your perspective is good and would of loved to see it in good focus.</td>', 'Hi, I like your photograph for several reasons. The shadows are nice giving lines and making the overall photograph more interesting and your lighting is good. But the focus seems to be off. Maybe camera shake, I dont know but it seems not to be crisp. Your perspective is good and would of loved to see it in good focus.', '2004-12-09 12:22:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054341, 125971, 22970, '<td valign="top">Good Shot! I like your perspective. I just wish the sky was not so burned out.</td>', 'Good Shot! I like your perspective. I just wish the sky was not so burned out.', '2004-12-09 12:23:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1054347, 126159, 16636, '<td valign="top">cool colours</td>', 'cool colours', '2004-12-09 12:33:08.000000', NULL, 1),
