(1059098, 126038, 6130, '<td valign="top">I love it.</td>', 'I love it.', '2004-12-13 02:21:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1059107, 126184, 24486, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a well deserved 10th place. I''m a little surprised to read that the Opera House is more popular than the bridge. I thought this was excellant &amp; I really loved your perspective. The fact that you got the Sydney Opera House in the shot as well, I thought was a bonus.</td>', 'Congratulations on a well deserved 10th place. I''m a little surprised to read that the Opera House is more popular than the bridge. I thought this was excellant & I really loved your perspective. The fact that you got the Sydney Opera House in the shot as well, I thought was a bonus.', '2004-12-13 02:36:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1059108, 126211, 3524, '<td valign="top">Thank you for all the valuable input. I did worry about that vertical perspective making the observatory, trees and other building appear to be leaning toward center. Part of me liked the way it looked like everything was reaching for the stars, but it also tempted to be distracting.<br/> <br/>KDO, the bulk of the foreground lighting in the image came from moonlight that was giving a beautiful glow to the whole facility. I had to use masks to separate the sky from the foreground to boost the contrast enough to give the impression of what I could see in the sky, at the same time the moon was bathing everything else. Based on some good comments here, I probably opened things up a bit too much. I worry sometimes that I make my images too dark...so I think I overcompensated.<br/> <br/>Thanks again!</td>', 'Thank you for all the valuable input. I did worry about that vertical perspective making the observatory, trees and other building appear to be leaning toward center. Part of me liked the way it looked like everything was reaching for the stars, but it also tempted to be distracting. KDO, the bulk of the foreground lighting in the image came from moonlight that was giving a beautiful glow to the whole facility. I had to use masks to separate the sky from the foreground to boost the contrast enough to give the impression of what I could see in the sky, at the same time the moon was bathing everything else. Based on some good comments here, I probably opened things up a bit too much. I worry sometimes that I make my images too dark...so I think I overcompensated. Thanks again!', '2004-12-13 02:37:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(1059131, 125627, 4090, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your first blue. Stunning photo</td>', 'Congratulations on your first blue. Stunning photo', '2004-12-13 03:05:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(1059134, 126240, 4090, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, great photo and set up</td>', 'Congratulations, great photo and set up', '2004-12-13 03:06:54.000000', NULL, 0),
