(1059370, 126240, 24925, '<td valign="top">To be honest, I really don''t like the "set up" aspect of photography and I think it''s interesting that the attitude on this site seems to be more about the end than the means BUT:<br/> <br/>When you''re this good, EddyG you need to flaunt it, baby!!<br/> <br/>Great work and effort!<br/> <br/>(Please let the positive part outweigh the the negative part of my comment)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-12-13 10:40:34.</i></td>', 'To be honest, I really don''t like the "set up" aspect of photography and I think it''s interesting that the attitude on this site seems to be more about the end than the means BUT: When you''re this good, EddyG you need to flaunt it, baby!! Great work and effort! (Please let the positive part outweigh the the negative part of my comment)', '2004-12-13 08:03:29.000000', '2004-12-13 10:40:34.000000', 0),
(1059381, 125627, 23458, '<td valign="top">Well would you look at that. I was right for once. I''m quite chuffed about that. Hey, if you can''t win a ribbon you can at least predict who will. Just to try and drag you down from the tall pedestal, this was only my second favourite image of the challenge :P.<br/> <br/>Brilliant work.</td>', 'Well would you look at that. I was right for once. I''m quite chuffed about that. Hey, if you can''t win a ribbon you can at least predict who will. Just to try and drag you down from the tall pedestal, this was only my second favourite image of the challenge :P. Brilliant work.', '2004-12-13 08:09:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(1059391, 125627, 8860, '<td valign="top">I have become extremely moist viewing these comments. I do thank each and every one of you who has spent the time to do so.  <br/>: )<br/> <br/>Thanks especially to those who made me laugh aloud: Bod, Gordon ("geewhy"), Manic. <br/> <br/>And samtrundle - you forsaw the future!<br/> <br/><i>Edit: forgot to mention how chuffed I was too, considering the quality of the rest of the field.</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-12-13 08:19:01.</i></td>', 'I have become extremely moist viewing these comments. I do thank each and every one of you who has spent the time to do so.  : ) Thanks especially to those who made me laugh aloud: Bod, Gordon ("geewhy"), Manic.  And samtrundle - you forsaw the future! Edit: forgot to mention how chuffed I was too, considering the quality of the rest of the field.', '2004-12-13 08:16:48.000000', '2004-12-13 08:19:01.000000', 0),
