(1067009, 126240, 30049, '<td valign="top">I really enjoyed your photo/composition (see comments during voting).  Last night at the library I was thumbing thru an older version of "The Joy Of Photography" and came across a photo by Pete Turner taken in 1980 that I thought you would find interesting (it was a bugger to find on the internet).  Getty Images has it...here''s a URL that should display it, if not the image number is 202780, or search under Pete Turner and it comes up on the first page (of 26!).<br/> <br/><a href="//creative.gettyimages.com/source/classes/FrameSet.aspx?&amp;pk=4&amp;source=front&amp;lightboxView=1&amp;txtSearch=202780" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Link</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by EddyG - Edited link -- (BTW, that photo is terrific!).</i></td>', 'I really enjoyed your photo/composition (see comments during voting).  Last night at the library I was thumbing thru an older version of "The Joy Of Photography" and came across a photo by Pete Turner taken in 1980 that I thought you would find interesting (it was a bugger to find on the internet).  Getty Images has it...here''s a URL that should display it, if not the image number is 202780, or search under Pete Turner and it comes up on the first page (of 26!). LinkMessage edited by EddyG - Edited link -- (BTW, that photo is terrific!).', '2004-12-17 11:24:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1067131, 126240, 30817, '<td valign="top">What a great idea. The effects of the TV sky add just enough softness to link up to the foreground.  Creativity pays sometimes, the other times, it is just a good idea.</td>', 'What a great idea. The effects of the TV sky add just enough softness to link up to the foreground.  Creativity pays sometimes, the other times, it is just a good idea.', '2004-12-17 13:53:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1067381, 125627, 7857, '<td valign="top">I''ve just been on my works Christmas party and it was a boat trip down the Thames... I was out on deck taking some photos and I was waiting to see this exact shot go by! You did an awsome job, the long exposure''s had a great effect on the water, and the colours are fantastic. Great job (clearly!)</td>', 'I''ve just been on my works Christmas party and it was a boat trip down the Thames... I was out on deck taking some photos and I was waiting to see this exact shot go by! You did an awsome job, the long exposure''s had a great effect on the water, and the colours are fantastic. Great job (clearly!)', '2004-12-17 17:48:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1067427, 125587, 3087, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Initial thoughts</b> <br/>I like the intensity of colours that come from the longish night-time exposure and the viewpoint creates an unusual composition.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/ Content</b> <br/>The content is certainly interesting as it provides an unusual look at a building that''s been photographed so many times before. That in itself is an achievement not to be sneezed at. <br/>I particularly like the strong linear aspect to the content  pale vertical lines at the left, bluey diagonal ones to the right and yellow horizontal ones (broken by verticals) in the centre which combine to create another vertical. The repetition of patterns is interesting. <br/>I am bothered by the way that the silver pipe to the far left seems to be quite far off the vertical as that jars with the more precise nature of such a structure, for me.<br/>The colours seem both saturated and strong and yet there is a feeling of muteness to the image  perhaps that''s more of a psychological reaction to the thought of the building during night-time.<br/> <br/><b>Background</b> <br/>The warm, natural, orangey colour of the sky works well against the more obviously man-made silvers and blues of the buidling.<br/> <br/><b>Camera Work - Technical</b> <br/>Nice colour and detail captured. <br/> <br/><b>Digital Processing - Technical</b> <br/>Nothing that stands out. The artifacts mentioned in one of your existing comments aren''t evident to me.<br/> <br/><b>Fits The Challenge</b> <br/>Yes.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion On The Photo</b> <br/>An interesting geometric abstract based on a famous landmark.<br/></td>', 'Critique Club  Initial thoughts I like the intensity of colours that come from the longish night-time exposure and the viewpoint creates an unusual composition. Composition/ Content The content is certainly interesting as it provides an unusual look at a building that''s been photographed so many times before. That in itself is an achievement not to be sneezed at. I particularly like the strong linear aspect to the content  pale vertical lines at the left, bluey diagonal ones to the right and yellow horizontal ones (broken by verticals) in the centre which combine to create another vertical. The repetition of patterns is interesting. I am bothered by the way that the silver pipe to the far left seems to be quite far off the vertical as that jars with the more precise nature of such a structure, for me.The colours seem both saturated and strong and yet there is a feeling of muteness to the image  perhaps that''s more of a psychological reaction to the thought of the building during night-time. Background The warm, natural, orangey colour of the sky works well against the more obviously man-made silvers and blues of the buidling. Camera Work - Technical Nice colour and detail captured.  Digital Processing - Technical Nothing that stands out. The artifacts mentioned in one of your existing comments aren''t evident to me. Fits The Challenge Yes. My Opinion On The Photo An interesting geometric abstract based on a famous landmark.', '2004-12-17 18:56:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1067745, 126240, 20236, '<td valign="top">I live 20 Mins from Stonehendge and i didn''t notice it was a fake!!!</td>', 'I live 20 Mins from Stonehendge and i didn''t notice it was a fake!!!', '2004-12-18 03:04:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1070526, 126143, 30584, '<td valign="top">As a fellow Okie, and shooter of the memorial myself, I have to say your balance of all the elements and colors is great! I especially love the color on the chairs, and the way the reflecting wall seems continuous with its reflection.</td>', 'As a fellow Okie, and shooter of the memorial myself, I have to say your balance of all the elements and colors is great! I especially love the color on the chairs, and the way the reflecting wall seems continuous with its reflection.', '2004-12-20 11:45:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1085236, 126240, 21101, '<td valign="top">Too Funny and waaaaay too clever!!<br/> <br/>Good show!!<br/></td>', 'Too Funny and waaaaay too clever!! Good show!!', '2005-01-01 11:22:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1118647, 125225, 12611, '<td valign="top">great shot; simple, powerful. nice.</td>', 'great shot; simple, powerful. nice.', '2005-01-19 07:44:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1132187, 126065, 656, '<td valign="top">Reminds me of an Ent from the Lord of the Rings, in many ways - with the almost ''arm-like'' branches.  <br/> <br/>Compositionally being a bit lower might also work, to isolate the tree more against the sky and increase the size with some perspective.  You might struggle to retain the sweep of the road, but getting close to the center line might really emphasize/ dramatize that sweep along with the tree- probably then becomes a portrait orientation shot too. <br/> <br/>Technically to my eye it looks a bit over sharpened and over saturated - there is some haloing on the horizon and around the tree branches, and the yellow/brown parts of the tree appear to be oversaturated to the point of losing some detail ?  (you can see this in levels in Photoshop btw)</td>', 'Reminds me of an Ent from the Lord of the Rings, in many ways - with the almost ''arm-like'' branches.   Compositionally being a bit lower might also work, to isolate the tree more against the sky and increase the size with some perspective.  You might struggle to retain the sweep of the road, but getting close to the center line might really emphasize/ dramatize that sweep along with the tree- probably then becomes a portrait orientation shot too.  Technically to my eye it looks a bit over sharpened and over saturated - there is some haloing on the horizon and around the tree branches, and the yellow/brown parts of the tree appear to be oversaturated to the point of losing some detail ?  (you can see this in levels in Photoshop btw)', '2005-01-26 00:03:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1137672, 125425, 20779, '<td valign="top">Terrific blending of persepctive, form and color. Excellent work!</td>', 'Terrific blending of persepctive, form and color. Excellent work!', '2005-01-28 18:49:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1153967, 126295, 1617, '<td valign="top">I like how you didn''t just foucs on the building</td>', 'I like how you didn''t just foucs on the building', '2005-02-07 00:07:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(1183444, 125284, 33560, '<td valign="top">This one creeps up on you.  It''s not striking or crisp, but the low contrast and literal dullness of the photo manages to convey the dullness of the day.  I like it that you have to do a bit of work to see the tower.  There''s something about the random placement of lighting standards that really disturbs the serenity of the setting and I think it detracts from the photo.  But if this photo had been taken by one of the great photographers of all time, this might be seen as a kind of statement about how our best intentioned and best executed attempts to control and improve our environment sometimes take an aesthetic toll.</td>', 'This one creeps up on you.  It''s not striking or crisp, but the low contrast and literal dullness of the photo manages to convey the dullness of the day.  I like it that you have to do a bit of work to see the tower.  There''s something about the random placement of lighting standards that really disturbs the serenity of the setting and I think it detracts from the photo.  But if this photo had been taken by one of the great photographers of all time, this might be seen as a kind of statement about how our best intentioned and best executed attempts to control and improve our environment sometimes take an aesthetic toll.', '2005-02-20 07:18:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1213659, 125054, 31738, '<td valign="top">Vince, I was just looking at this photo and I have to say the colors are awesome. The sun was just right and you picked a great day for this shot. That 20D is insaneee LOL.</td>', 'Vince, I was just looking at this photo and I have to say the colors are awesome. The sun was just right and you picked a great day for this shot. That 20D is insaneee LOL.', '2005-03-07 21:03:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1220869, 125054, 2741, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gtroia:</b></div><hr/><i> Vince, I was just looking at this photo and I have to say the colors are awesome. The sun was just right and you picked a great day for this shot. That 20D is insaneee LOL. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes.. the sun was just right, and it was pretty early too. I actually got over to Coney Island that day at about 6:30am, so I can wait for the sun to come up. I wanted to get the right kind of light.</td>', 'Originally posted by gtroia: Vince, I was just looking at this photo and I have to say the colors are awesome. The sun was just right and you picked a great day for this shot. That 20D is insaneee LOL.   Yes.. the sun was just right, and it was pretty early too. I actually got over to Coney Island that day at about 6:30am, so I can wait for the sun to come up. I wanted to get the right kind of light.', '2005-03-10 21:17:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1254697, 125967, 7863, '<td valign="top">rkligman, just because you don''t appriciate towers don''t make it a dull subject. I think it is a great shot. I for one know it is almost impossible to photograph towers. Great job!</td>', 'rkligman, just because you don''t appriciate towers don''t make it a dull subject. I think it is a great shot. I for one know it is almost impossible to photograph towers. Great job!', '2005-03-28 17:56:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1523092, 125728, 15711, '<td valign="top">Stunning use of light.  The angle of the shot is excellent as well.</td>', 'Stunning use of light.  The angle of the shot is excellent as well.', '2005-07-10 11:50:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1539088, 125728, 35517, '<td valign="top">WOW.... speechless... perfection....!!</td>', 'WOW.... speechless... perfection....!!', '2005-07-16 10:19:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1563620, 126207, 37740, '<td valign="top">What a great piece of architecture! The lines a stunning. Love it.</td>', 'What a great piece of architecture! The lines a stunning. Love it.', '2005-07-26 07:54:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1677530, 125627, 34659, '<td valign="top">I don''t know how I missed this shot - HOLY CRAP!  I can''t believe the sharpness and deepness of the tones.  Truly incredible and one of the best images I''ve seen on this site.  Outstanding.</td>', 'I don''t know how I missed this shot - HOLY CRAP!  I can''t believe the sharpness and deepness of the tones.  Truly incredible and one of the best images I''ve seen on this site.  Outstanding.', '2005-09-05 23:48:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1677775, 125627, 15711, '<td valign="top">What a beautiful image.  The cool blues and grays in the night sky are simply awesome.  Stunning view!!</td>', 'What a beautiful image.  The cool blues and grays in the night sky are simply awesome.  Stunning view!!', '2005-09-06 01:19:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1679143, 125791, 43463, '<td valign="top">The stark white background along with the barren trees in the background really adds to the imagery that you wish to portray here: a cold, stark, and empty world. The statue carries another figure and on the face we can clearly see the anguish crafted into it''s face. All elements combine to make us ''see'' a little of the pain and suffering that occured during Ireland''s Great Potato Famine.</td>', 'The stark white background along with the barren trees in the background really adds to the imagery that you wish to portray here: a cold, stark, and empty world. The statue carries another figure and on the face we can clearly see the anguish crafted into it''s face. All elements combine to make us ''see'' a little of the pain and suffering that occured during Ireland''s Great Potato Famine.', '2005-09-06 14:36:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1811988, 125969, 38706, '<td valign="top">I like that you found a different angle from the mainstream - tough with  that and the coathanger since they have been done to death.  Makes me a little home sick also, which makes a good pic when somebody else gets meaning out of it.</td>', 'I like that you found a different angle from the mainstream - tough with  that and the coathanger since they have been done to death.  Makes me a little home sick also, which makes a good pic when somebody else gets meaning out of it.', '2005-10-25 20:26:37.000000', NULL, 0),
